messages:
samir: quick question — for chat/completions streaming deltas: should the server ever emit a `role` field after the initial delta? some clients crash if they see `role` midway.

jess: no, role should only appear on the first chunk for that message (we documented that but it's easy to miss).

kevin: oof — which doc? i can add a clarification note. also what about `function_call` updates while streaming? we have clients that expect `function_call.name` then later `function_call.arguments`.

maria: yes, function_call can be incremental. intended shape is: first chunk may set `function_call.name`, subsequent chunks add `function_call.arguments` (string pieces) and finally the non-streamed final event resolves it. but we should be explicit about ordering. :thinking:

samir: failing client example: it expects the first object to contain role + full text. when it sees role again it treats it as a new message. we should call it out.

jess: proposal: clearly state these rules in the contract and add a small streaming example block. something like:

```
// server-sent chunks (ndjson style)
{"delta": {"role": "assistant"}}
{"delta": {"content": "Hello"}}
{"delta": {"content": " world"}}
{"delta": {"function_call": {"name": "get_weather"}}}
{"delta": {"function_call": {"arguments": "{\"city\": \"S"}}}
{"delta": {"function_call": {"arguments": "an Francisco\"}"}} 
{"done": true, "final": {"function_call": {"name": "get_weather", "arguments": "{\"city\": \"San Francisco\"}"}}}
```

jess: note: `role` only first line; `content` and `function_call.arguments` can be chunked; final envelope has canonical resolved object.

kevin: should we include a `delta_type` hint like `role|content|func` to reduce parsing fragility for naive clients?

maria: prefer minimal additions — adding new required fields hurts older clients. we can add `delta_type` as optional. and emphasize that clients MUST concatenate `function_call.arguments` strings in order.

schemabot: note: PR #1247 opened to add streaming examples & backwards-compat section (link: https://git.redwood/eng/stream-spec/pull/1247) :robot_face:

samir: perfect. one more edge: empty `content` chunks (heartbeat) — allowed? we have proxies that drop empty lines.

jess: we should avoid empty `delta` objects. if it's a heartbeat, send a comment line or a small keepalive event like `{"keepalive":true}` so proxies preserve it.

kevin: ok i'll draft the doc change and add the ndjson example. tagging @maria to review the function_call wording — can you take a pass?

maria: taking it now, will push suggestions inline.

samir: thanks — once merged i'll coordinate a short note for SDKs so they can handle role/function_call streaming correctly. :thumbsup:
